 Huckabee Sanders (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Arkansas is one of the most Republican-leaning states on the 2026 map, and Governor Sarah Huckabee Sanders is running for a second term with the full weight of incumbency behind her. Her Democratic challenger, state Senator Fredrick Love, is a low-profile candidate with no visible fundraising or outside support, and a Libertarian is also on the ballot. The October Hendrix College poll showed Sanders leading 51-32, and every major race rater rates the contest Solid or Safe Republican. Prediction markets give Democrats only a 1-3 percent chance.\n\nThe forecast expects Sanders to win by roughly 16 points, consistent with the state's partisan lean plus her incumbency advantage. There is little evidence of a competitive race, and uncertainty is modest given the consistency of the available signals.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0236, "margin": -11.99}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0374, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0306, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0358, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0294, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.026, "margin": -13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0389, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0411, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0419, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.0317, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0391, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0323, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0322, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0188, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0177, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0223, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_d